Note that $(-1)^{i-2}\binom{d-3}{i-2}\equiv (\binom i2-\binom {i+1}3)d+\binom i2 \,\,\pmod{  d^2+d},\forall i\ge 2$.

From (\ref{d-g-2}) and (\ref{d-g-3}), we have (\ref{d-g-4}) hold for any $i\ge 2$. It is clear that (\ref{d-g-4}) holds for $i=1$.



