Suppose that $D(M)$ is a compact space. It is clear that $EC(M^{\#})=%
%TCIMACRO{\dbigcup \limits_{m\in M^{\#}}}%
%BeginExpansion
{\displaystyle\bigcup\limits_{m\in M^{\#}}}
%EndExpansion
U_{m}$. It means that there exists $m_{1},m_{2},\ldots,m_{n}\in M^{\#}$ such that
$EC(M^{\#})=%
%TCIMACRO{\dbigcup \limits_{i=1}^{n}}%
%BeginExpansion
{\displaystyle\bigcup\limits_{i=1}^{n}}
%EndExpansion
U_{m_{i}}.\ $Now, choose an element $Rz\in\left\{  Rm\right\}  _{m\in M^{\#}%
}\ $then $z\in M^{\#}$ and $\left[  z\right]  \in EC(M^{\#})=%
%TCIMACRO{\dbigcup \limits_{i=1}^{n}}%
