\section{Conclusions}
In this paper, based on the technique in Reference \cite{2022A}, we generalize it and apply the diagonalization-based direct time-parallel algorithm to solve time-dependent differential equations of order 1 to 3. We derive the one-time systems for  $\boldsymbol{u}$  of order 1 to 3 and provide explicit formulas for diagonalization. We also prove the condition number  $cond\left( V \right) =\mathcal{O} \left( n^3 \right)$  of the eigenvector matrix  $V$  corresponding to the time discretization matrix  $B$ . In the experiment on the fast spectral decomposition algorithm for matrix  $B$ , it is observed that due to the influence of the condition number of  $V$ , when  $n$  is large,  $w_{fast}$  is not ideal. However, it can be seen from  $\eta _{fast}$  that the eigenvalues obtained by the fast algorithm are basically consistent with those calculated by the  $eig$  function in MATLAB. In addition, we also present a fast algorithm for the eigenvector matrix $V^{-1}$, which can effectively accelerate the computational efficiency when applied to the fast spectral decomposition algorithm of the time-discrete matrix $B$. Finally, we use two second-order equations and two third-order equations to illustrate the feasibility of our one-time system.

