    \caption{Average number of ancestral chromosomes that possess extant genetic material, for different population sizes (left) and chromosome lengths (right), still with $r = 1/L_c$. The computations of \cite{wiuf_nbancestors_1997} are valid for one chromosome per individual, and again we multiplied the prediction by $72$. Temporal data of the number of ancestral chromosomes in our simulations are provided in the Supp. \autoref{fig:temp_nb_chranc}.}
