Finally, we analyze the case where the price impact parameter is set to $\gamma_1 = 0$ in regime $1$ and $\gamma_2 = 0.33$ in regime $2$. We fix $q_1 = 0.2$ and vary $q_2$, allowing us to study how the asymmetry in regime-switching probabilities affects execution. 
