			%			Letting $n\to\infty$ and combining the above estimates, we obtain that $(\tilde{\nu},\tilde{K})$ is a solution to (\ref{mdp1}). Thanks to the uniqueness of the solutions of (\ref{mdp1}) we can deduce that $\tilde{\nu}=\nu^\psi$, which completes the proof.
