\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:Conclusion}
In this study, we have presented a novel methodology to model cyber attacks, analyse their paths through exploitable vulnerabilities, and evaluate the impact of cyber exploits on services in an enterprise or infrastructure network. Our model takes into account interconnected dependencies across different network layers, from the physical layer to the application layer. Here, we have employed probabilistic approaches to analyse how cyber attacks propagate through attack graphs and their effects on user services and application layers in communication networks. Our graph-based modelling approach proved to be versatile, as it can be used to investigate cyber threats and attacks at various levels of detail. This methodology also allows the evaluation of different cyber attack scenarios and supports the evaluation of protection and mitigation measures.

In addition, our method for modelling cyber threats and attacks enables the planning and implementation of tailored protective actions, taking into account the importance of services as experienced by users. The proposed methodology helps security specialists and system administrators make well-informed decisions regarding risk mitigation strategies.

