    \subsection{Autoencoder Spectra}
    We now look at whether the trained autoencoder spectra is an adequate representation of the sea state, i.e., whether the variability of all samples within a bin can be attributed to the sampling variance. 
    In this case a given $H_s$--$T_e$ bin is subdivided into multiple $\theta_1$--$\theta_2$ bins. 
