    Qualitatively, we can say that the variability of the samples within each bin can be attributed to sampling variance, with most samples falling within the $95\%$ confidence interval.
    This suggests the use of these 4-parameters is adequate to capture spectra variability. 
    The autoencoder spectra captures the mean of the samples well for each bin, whereas a single Pierson-Moskowitz spectrum does not. 
