\subsection{Suspense and Surprise Trends in the Italian Serie A and French Ligue 1}

Figure \ref{fig:suspense_surprise_isa} in Appendix \ref{sec:timetrendapp} presents box plots for the top teams, Juventus, Napoli, and Internazionale, alongside the averages of all other teams in the Italian Serie A. Figure \ref{fig:suspense_isa} shows that suspense values in the 2010/11 season were initially clustered closely together, , just around the lower bound of the benchmark range. Over time, particularly in matches involving Juventus, suspense values regularly fell below the benchmark. Toward the end of the sample period, suspense values appear to converge again, with most teams falling within the benchmark range, except for Internazionale, which won the 2023/24 season by a margin of 19 points. Interestingly, in 2023/24, Juventus recorded the highest suspense values among all teams, well within the benchmark range.

With regard to surprise, Figure \ref{fig:surprise_isa} shows that values remained consistently within the benchmark range, and no top team ever generated surprise values significantly below it. The linear regression results in Table \ref{tab:time_trends_isa} in Appendix \ref{sec:timetrendapp} do not indicate any notable trends in Serie A, except for a decline in both suspense and surprise in matches involving Internazionale, with estimated decreases of 2.2\% and 2.0\% per season, respectively.

In the French Ligue 1, only suspense values in matches involving Paris Saint-Germain frequently fall significantly below the lower bound of the benchmark range (see Figure \ref{fig:suspense_surprise_fl1} in Appendix \ref{sec:timetrendapp}). Similar patterns are observed for surprise, although the differences are not statistically significant. Linear regressions reveal a significant negative trend in both suspense (approximately 3.1\% decrease per season) and surprise (approximately 2.4\% decrease per season) for matches involving Paris Saint-Germain, with no changes observed for other teams (see Table \ref{tab:time_trends_fl1}).


