Using the obtained values for refractive index (\(n\)), new materials were defined within the EM simulations for the QGAN-based metasurface design process. It is essential to recognize that conventional manufacturing methodologies may prove inadequate for the novel materials produced via this approach. The material definition framework allows the model to explore more design possibilities by predicting a wider range of material properties, which might otherwise be overlooked if simplified into fixed categories.
