\subsection{A deterministic percolation transition in the logistic GOL}\label{sec:cluster_analysis}

Motivated by the interesting asymptotic behavior of the size of the largest cluster in the logistic GOL, we here complement these findings by studying the cluster dynamics of the system as $\lambda$ approaches $\lambda_P=0.86055$ \textit{from below}. By investigating the sizes and geometrical properties of clusters, we find that $\lambda_P$ is the critical point of a percolation transition that separates two distinct phases of asymptotic behavior: a dynamic phase with no spanning cluster ($\lambda\leq\lambda_P$) and a dynamic phase with a giant vacuum cluster that spans the lattice ($\lambda_P<\lambda<\lambda_A$). 

