 In Fig. \ref{fig:purities} $\Etrccclb$ is plotted versus $R$ for a symmetric binary $Q(x)$ and different values of purity $\Pur$. For a given rate, the exponent $\Etrclb$ becomes smaller as the purity decreases. Also the rate $R^*$ below which the exponent $\Etrccclb$ is strictly larger than $\Er(R)$ shows the same trend, going from $0.025$ for $\Pur=0.9$ to $0.003$ for $\Pur=0.7$.
